1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-9","children":[[["$","section","What the lender is actually assessing",{"id":"what-the-lender-is-actually-assessing","className":"mb-12 last:mb-0","data-reveal":true,"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[1.65rem] leading-snug text-[var(--sheet-ink)] sm:text-[2rem]","children":"What the lender is actually assessing"}],[["$","p","Three things decide a plot loan: the bor",{"className":"mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--sheet-soft)]","children":"Three things decide a plot loan: the borrower, the land, and the exit. The borrower is income and credit history. The land is title, approval and access — lenders publish lists of approved layouts and reject plots in unapproved or agriculturally classified land. The exit is how the lender could recover the money if you default, which is why an approachable, sanctioned layout in a recognised corridor is financed more readily than an isolated parcel."}],["$","p","Because of that third point, plot loans ",{"className":"mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--sheet-soft)]","children":"Because of that third point, plot loans commonly finance a lower share of the property value than a home loan, and over a shorter tenure. Ask the lender for the current figures for your case rather than relying on a rate card."}]],"$undefined","$undefined"]}],["$","section","Documents a lender will ask for",{"id":"documents-a-lender-will-ask-for","className":"mb-12 last:mb-0","data-reveal":true,"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[1.65rem] leading-snug text-[var(--sheet-ink)] sm:text-[2rem]","children":"Documents a lender will ask for"}],"$undefined",["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 max-w-[68ch] space-y-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--sheet-ink)]","children":[["$","li","KYC: identity, address and PAN.",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 sh